{
 "schema": "trust-cg-wasm-corpus-v1",
 "notes": [
  "The wasm-vs-llvm corpus: the source of truth for the program set. run.py refuses to run (exit 2) when progs/*.rs and this manifest disagree or a file's SHA-256 differs from its row.",
  "Every program is a #![no_std] cdylib whose #[no_mangle] extern \"C\" exports take and return only i32/i64/f32/f64 scalars, whose loops are bounded independently of their inputs, and whose panic handler traps on wasm32. They come from this project's wasm32 Rust-level differential campaigns and were selected because they agreed with rustc+LLVM at -C opt-level=2 when the wasm32 performance plan was written; every harness run checks that agreement again.",
  "`group` names the campaign a program came from (float, int, slice, kernels); it is a label, not a gate category.",
  "Changing the program set (adding, removing or renaming a program) changes the ledger rows' program-set digest: the ratchet compares the shared programs and reports the rest INCONCLUSIVE until `scripts/check_perf_ratchet.py --append --new-lineage '<reason>'` records a new lineage on an eligible evidence row. Editing a program's source changes its sha256 here and the corpus manifest digest stamped in provenance.",
  "`soft_signed_zero` lists, per program, the exports whose +0.0/-0.0 results Rust leaves unspecified, each with its reason; the harness accepts (and records) a signed-zero difference from B1 only on those exports. Every other signed-zero difference is a disagreement. NaN payloads are not observed."
 ],
